		"habit": "a loose tuft 15 to 30 cm tall in leaf; flowering stems 30 to 60 cm, so the panicles stand at about twice the leaf height. Leaf mass about as wide as tall; with the stems, about 1.3 times as tall as wide. Widest at the arching blade tips, about a third of the way up. Outline: a loose fountain of blades under a spray of slender stems. Many tillers from one crown, spreading by short rhizomes.",
		"branching": "none. Tillers from the crown; each tiller a stack of sheaths with two to four blades set alternately in two ranks. The panicle branches in whorls of three to five at each node.",
		"leaves": "simple flat blades 2 to 4 mm wide and 10 to 30 cm long (about fifty to eighty times as long as wide), even in width almost to the end, then closing in a short blunt boat-shaped (hooded) tip. Two pale lines (tram-lines) either side of the midrib on the upper face. Margin entire, finely rough. Soft, bright to mid green above, slightly glossy keel below. Short blunt ligule at the collar.",
